{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PlanarEmbedding"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"G"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","text":"Graph"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A self-loop appears twice in its vertex’s order, its two ends adjacent, enclosing a face of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"length 1. Parallel copies sit side by side, each consecutive pair enclosing a face of length 2."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Each clockwise order starts at the first edge of "},{"code":"incidentEdges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Faces."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" The face after the half-edge from u along edge e to w continues with the half-edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before e in the clockwise order at w, so a face lies to the right of each of its half-edges.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Faces are counted per connected component, and an isolated vertex has none: two disjoint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"triangles have four faces.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The embedding keeps the graph it was made from (copy-on-write, so O(1)); mutating the graph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"afterwards does not change it. When a graph has several embeddings, which one is returned is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not specified, but it depends only on the graph’s rows: graphs with the same vertices, the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edge positions and the same incidence order get the same embedding.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Structure","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding.swift#L66","fileName":"PlanarEmbedding.swift"},"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:9Planarity15PlanarEmbeddingV","modules":[{"name":"Planarity"}],"symbolKind":"struct","title":"PlanarEmbedding","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PlanarEmbedding","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PlanarEmbedding"}]},"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/ClockwiseIncidentEdges","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/ClockwiseNeighborIndices","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/ClockwiseNeighbors","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/Faces-swift.struct"],"anchor":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/faceCount","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/faces-swift.property"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/clockwiseIncidentEdges(checked:)","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/clockwiseIncidentEdges(of:)","doc:\/\/Planarity\/documentation\/Planarity\/PlanarEmbedding\/clockwiseNeighborIndice